-- Schema 4 → 5. A manual rank for the cards inside one board group.
--
-- Preserves data, as everything after 1.sqm must. This one preserves it the easy
-- way: it adds nothing but a column with a default.
--
-- ── Why this one does NOT rebuild `issues` ──────────────────────────────────
--
-- 2.sqm and 3.sqm both did, and both had to: they added columns with COMPOSITE
-- foreign keys, which ALTER TABLE cannot express. `sort_order` references
-- nothing. It is a plain integer with a non-null default, which is exactly the
-- shape SQLite allows to be added in place — so there is no new table, no copy,
-- no DROP, and therefore none of the cascade danger that forced the
-- foreign-keys-off migration path in the first place. See Database.kt.
--
-- (It still runs on that connection, because openDatabase does the schema work
-- there unconditionally. It simply does not need it.)
--
-- ── Why every row starts at 0 ───────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- 0 means "never ranked", and a group in which everything is 0 sorts by
-- `updated_at DESC` alone — which is precisely what every board did before this
-- column existed. So this migration changes the order of nothing: it makes a new
-- order *possible* without imposing one. The first drag on a group is what gives
-- that group ranks 1..n. See Issues.sq's sort_order.
ALTER TABLE issues ADD COLUMN sort_order INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
